# TASK
Extract durable facts about the user from one message.

# RULES
- Only what the user said about themselves. Do not invent or infer.
- A question, a request, a discussion or task text is not a fact.
- When the message names a time ("moved in March 2026"), add a "valid_from" field with that time as
  "2026-03" or "2026-03-01". When no time is named, there must be no "valid_from" field.
- A fact that fits none of the predicates goes into notes as one short phrase.
- The subject is almost always "user".
- At most three facts per message.
- Write value and sentence in the language of the message.

# PREDICATES
lives_in — where the user lives
works_at — the employer
works_as — the job title
studied_at — where the user studied
born_in — the place of birth
born_on — the date of birth
has_pet — a pet
likes — something the user likes
dislikes — something the user avoids
speaks — a language the user speaks
owns — a durable thing the user owns
lives_with — who the user lives with
married_to — the spouse

# ALREADY KNOWN
{known_facts}

# MESSAGE
User: {user_message}
Assistant: {assistant_message}

# ANSWER
Return ONE JSON object, no prose and no markdown:
{{"facts": [{{"subject": "user", "predicate": "lives_in", "value": "Tbilisi", "sentence": "Lives in Tbilisi", "valid_from": "2026-03", "confidence": 0.9}}], "notes": []}}
When there is nothing, return {{"facts": [], "notes": []}}.
